course: dictionary
lesson: 402
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. «Appearance» can mean how someone looks, when something comes into sight, taking part in an event, or how something seems. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning the writer chose.
explain: «The Rat rows and the Mole steers, carefully, because the shadows on the water look «as solid to all appearance as the banks themselves».» Here appearance means how something seems. The shadows only look solid, so the clue is in the word seems and in the comparison with the real banks.
explain: «People look at the outward appearance, but the Lord looks at the heart.» Outward appearance means how someone looks from the outside. The word «but» is your clue: it sets the outside against the inside, the heart.
explain: A good check is to swap in a meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense. Appearances can fool us, so the sentence may describe how things seem, not how they really are.
fact: Appearance is a noun. You can write an appearance or appearances.
fact: «Appearance» can mean how someone looks, like their hair, face and clothes.
fact: «Appearance» can mean when someone or something comes into sight, especially suddenly.
fact: «Appearance» can mean taking part in a show, game or event, like an actor making an appearance on TV.
fact: Phrases include «judging by appearances» and «from all appearances», which often warn you that things may not be what they seem.
exercise: In science, describing the appearance of a rock means talking about its | Its owner | Its price | *Its colour, shape and texture | Its birthday
exercise: «It is an allegory, a story with a hidden meaning, not history: we might mistake appearances for the whole truth.» In this sentence, what do appearances mean? | A football game | The best clothes people wear | The arrival of a new family | *How things seem, which may not be the truth
exercise: A famous actor makes an appearance on a quiz show. What does appearance mean here? | *Taking part in the show as a guest | A way of dressing for the show | Painting the stage | Walking out of the show early
test: Samuel was told «People look at the outward appearance, but the Lord looks at the heart». What does outward appearance mean? | Where someone lives | *How someone looks from the outside | How someone feels inside | How loudly someone speaks
test: Dad says, «From all appearances, the sun is coming out.» What does from all appearances mean? | *How things seem, judging by what we can see | Going out to play | Photos of the sun | The sun's birthday
exam: Maya says appearance always means how someone looks. Is she right? | Yes, it only means clothes | Yes, it only means how a rock feels | No, it only means being late for school | *No, it can also mean arriving suddenly or taking part in an event
